cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the stored analysis outputs, please cite both
  the software (this record) and the article it accompanies.
title: >-
  How Stable Are Feature Rankings at Early Decision Points? A Comparison of
  Five Feature-Selection Methods with Student-Grouped Cross-Validation and a
  Later-Presentation Holdout (analysis code)
abstract: >-
  Code and stored outputs for a comparison of the stability of feature
  rankings from five feature-selection methods (ANOVA F-test, mutual
  information, LASSO path entry order, recursive feature elimination with
  XGBoost importances, and mean absolute SHAP values) on the Open University
  Learning Analytics Dataset at days 30, 60 and 90 of each presentation, with
  xAPI-Edu-Data as an end-of-term contrast. Includes student-grouped repeated
  cross-validation, a later-presentation holdout with student-cluster
  bootstrap intervals, a half-sampling bootstrap for the Nogueira stability
  index, disjoint-sample agreement within and between presentations, a
  marking-delay sensitivity analysis, and the per-fold, per-replicate and
  per-repeat outputs from which the reported tables and figures are
  regenerated.
